{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "The Capabilities Framework will extend the channel config by adding a capabilities map split into three levels: root channel, application, and orderer.",
    "Binaries not supporting required capabilities will crash intentionally to ensure data integrity and safety.",
    "The chaincode shim API will be extended with a new method `GetTrxState(key string)` to optionally enable Read-Your-Writes (RYW) during key retrieval.",
    "`MSPConfig` will be refactored into an interface to allow the construction of channel config blocks outside of the `configtxgen` tool.",
    "Assorted chaincode singletons will be removed and replaced with dependency injection or context-specific instances to facilitate future lifecycle work.",
    "The new lifecycle validation interface will return validation parameters for chaincodes, including a special auto-generated signature policy for '+lifecycle' requiring the majority of orgs to endorse."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer has prior experience and familiarity with the Hyperledger Fabric codebase and its architecture.",
    "Video recording and editing tools, as well as presentation software, are readily available for creating the documentation and video in U3.",
    "CouchDB is already integrated into the development environment for performance testing in U4.",
    "Unit and integration testing efforts are included within the estimates for each respective activity.",
    "No external dependencies or blockers will delay the development of these features."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Implement Capabilities Framework",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement the capabilities map in channel config (root, application, orderer). Modify channel config APIs and capabilities definitions. Implement crash mechanism for unsupported capabilities and upgrade enforcement logic.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Implement RYW for Chaincode Key Retrieval",
      "activity_description": "Extend the chaincode shim API with `stub.GetTrxState(key string)` and implement the logic to retrieve already updated keys during an active transaction.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Create Documentation and Video for Adding Organizations",
      "activity_description": "Create a presentation diagram and record a detailed video showing the process of adding additional organizations into a running network without bringing it down.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Implement CouchDB Query Performance Measurement",
      "activity_description": "Develop a tool or script to benchmark and measure the performance of Fabric queries when CouchDB is used as the state database, and document the results.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Refactor MSPConfig to Interface",
      "activity_description": "Change `MSPConfig` to an interface to allow the construction of custom channel config blocks outside of the `configtxgen` tool, and update related code accordingly.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Remove Chaincode Singletons",
      "activity_description": "Identify and refactor assorted chaincode singletons to make development and testing more reliable, preparing the codebase for new lifecycle work.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Generate Config Files from World Config in Tests",
      "activity_description": "Implement test setup logic to generate peer `core.yaml` and orderer `orderer.yaml` configuration files based on the values set in the World config.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Implement Lifecycle Validation Parameters Interface",
      "activity_description": "Implement the new lifecycle interface returning validation parameters for a chaincode, including the special edge case for '+lifecycle' with an auto-generated majority-of-orgs endorsement policy.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 196
  }
}
```

